# Params authored by this server. See `.local/content.sym` for why these live in
# `.local/` rather than the upstream symbol files.
#
# Id allocation: vanilla params occupy 0..~1935 and grow upward; RSMod's own params
# occupy 65386..65534 and grow *downward*. Ours start at 50000 and grow upward, in
# the middle of that gap, so neither side can reach us. Duplicate ids are only
# detected within a single file, so staying out of both bands is what keeps a
# future upstream param from silently aliasing one of ours.
50000	mining_pickaxe_success_rates
50001	firemaking_rate_low
50002	firemaking_rate_high
50003	firemaking_burn_ticks
50004	prayer_offer_xp_percent
50005	prayer_offer_keep_percent
50006	cooking_burnt
50007	cooking_stop_burn_fire
50008	cooking_stop_burn_range
50009	cooking_range_only
50010	cooking_name
50011	hunter_trap_kind
50012	hunter_rate_low
50013	hunter_rate_high
50014	hunter_creature_respawn
50015	hunter_loc_trapping
50016	hunter_loc_trapping_dirs
50017	hunter_loc_full
50018	hunter_secondary_product
50019	hunter_secondary_count
50020	hunter_trap_return

# Vanilla param 50, named here rather than built here.
#
# This is the one entry in this file that is NOT ours, and it deliberately sits outside the 50000
# band the header describes. Param 50 is a genuine Jagex param that `param.sym` dumps without a
# name, so `find()` cannot reach it; naming it in `.local/` is the only way to get a typed handle.
# The header's id-band rule guards against *accidentally* aliasing an upstream id -- here the alias
# onto 50 is the entire point, and `.local/` is merged over `symbols/`, so this resolves to the
# vanilla type rather than minting anything.
#
# It is the npc -> slayer task mapping, and it is what the whole Slayer skill hangs on: 2119 npc
# types carry it and its values are `slayer_task:id` in dbtable 113 (abyssal demon 42, kurask 45,
# gargoyle 46, dark beast 66, smoke devil 95). Declared INT with default 0 in the cache, so an npc
# that is nobody's task reads 0 for free.
50	slayer_task

# Vanilla param 880, named here rather than built here - the same exception as `slayer_task`
# above. It is a league relic struct's description (the HTML the relics screen's expanded view
# prints), and naming it is what lets `LeagueRelicDescriptions` rewrite it with a StructEditor.
880	league_relic_description
